# Compose-level config for the Docker deployment.
#
# You should not need this file: `node scripts/docker-setup.mjs` asks three questions and
# writes a .env for you. It is here for anyone who would rather write it by hand, and as the
# list of what the compose file actually reads.
#
# Separate from server/.env, which is the bare (no Docker) install's config.

# Where your projects live. Every directory directly inside it becomes a project.
# Mounted at the same path inside the container, not cosmetic, since tmux and claude run on
# the host, so paths have to mean the same thing on both sides. It is also HOME in the
# container, which is how Burrow finds ~/.claude and ~/.burrow.
BURROW_HOME=/root

# The port published on 127.0.0.1. Loopback only: Burrow hands a browser a shell on this
# machine, so it does not go on the open network by accident. The port INSIDE the container is
# always 8317 and is not affected by this.
BURROW_PORT=8317

# Who sessions run as on the host. The container is root, so leaving this unset means every
# session is root carrying the container's PATH, which finds none of your tools, and leaves
# root-owned files in your folders. Set, sessions start as a login shell for this user, so nvm
# and anything else in your profile works as it does in your own terminal.
BURROW_HOST_USER=

# --- Tailscale sidecar (optional) --------------------------------------------
# Publishes Burrow on your tailnet over HTTPS, with nothing open to the network. The service
# does not start at all unless COMPOSE_PROFILES says so, which is what lets a plain
# `docker compose up -d` work for someone who does not use Tailscale.
# COMPOSE_PROFILES=tailscale
# TS_AUTHKEY=          # a reusable key from login.tailscale.com/admin/settings/keys
# BURROW_TS_HOSTNAME=burrow    # the node name, and so the URL: https://burrow.<tailnet>.ts.net

# --- Claude authentication (optional, recommended) ---------------------------
# A token from `claude setup-token`. Without one, Terminal sessions still work and use the
# CLI's own /login, but with several sessions sharing one login, an expiry stops all of them
# at once, each waiting on input.
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=

# Optional extra shared secret in front of the whole app. Usually unnecessary.
# BURROW_TOKEN=
